        "statement_id": "statement:conclusion:body",
        "text": "One meaningful contrast in the reviewed record is that Foushee opposed six reviewed proposals that would displace specific D.C. public-safety rules and supported two reviewed terrorism-preparedness mandates. This contrast is not a complete explanation of the record: opposition to firearm-access barrier reduction and fraud-enforcement capacity expansion remains separately visible, and the mixed HALT Fentanyl episode limits any one-direction account."
